= Operating system — Simple =

An '''operating system''' is the software layer that manages a computer's hardware and gives programs useful services.

It helps programs use:

* the processor;
* memory;
* files and storage;
* devices;
* networks.

It also separates programs from one another and decides how resources are shared.

Windows, Linux, macOS, Android, and iOS are operating systems.

The kernel is the core part of an operating system, but the whole operating system usually includes much more than the kernel.

